      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To handle a roof insurance claim in Utah, document sudden storm damage (such as hail, high winds, or heavy snow/fallen debris), verify your policy's coverage terms, and file directly with your insurer before scheduling repairs.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Steps to File & Manage Your Claim"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect and prevent further damage: Check safely from the ground or attic for missing/lifted shingles, granules in gutters, or active leaks. Make temporary tarping/waterproofing repairs if needed to keep the home watertight.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review your policy terms: Check whether your roof is covered at Replacement Cost Value (RCV) or Actual Cash Value (ACV) (which deducts depreciation for age) and note your deductible. Sudden weather damage is typically covered, while normal wear and tear, age-related brittleness, or poor maintenance are generally excluded.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a local inspection: Have a licensed, local Utah roofer document damage with photos and measurements. You can also review guidance on Utah roof insurance claims to weigh filing yourself first and avoiding risky contract terms.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah roof insurance claims",
                "link": "https://www.google.com/url?sa=i&source=web&rct=j&url=https://writeforusroofing.com/does-a-utah-roofer-help-with-insurance-claims/&ved=2ahUKEwi7_redt6OYAxXFE1kFHZgOJekQy_kOegoIAggACAAIDRAO&opi=89978449&cd&psig=AOvVaw3IB00WGH9ue6mNP21bcvZS&ust=1795706793058000"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Open the claim & meet the adjuster: Call your insurer with your policy number, the date of the weather event, and a factual description of the damage. Keep descriptions focused on the event and visible damage rather than guessing fault or calling the roof \"old\".",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "If denied or underpaid: Request a written explanation, submit additional photos or a detailed contractor report, and ask for a reinspection or formal appeal.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
